Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:01.990 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  welcome back to cbs this morning  only on cbs this morning new findings  from a congressional investigation into  infant inclined sleepers finds that  fisher price  failed to ensure its rock and play was  safe  and ignored warnings it was dangerous  the rock n play was on the market for  about  10 years the consumer product safety  commission says it's linked to more than  30 infant deaths 4.7 million were sold  before a voluntary recall by the company  in 2019 consumer investigative  correspondent anna werner  got an exclusive look at the report from  the house committee on oversight and  reform  anna how was the rock and play allowed  on shelves  in the first place well good question  anthony you know these products weren't  regulated like  cradles and bassinets and now this new  report is calling out fisher price and  its parent company mattel  for selling what investigators call a  dangerous product  despite clear evidence it put infants at  risk of serious harm or  death this is outrageous  in my opinion it's criminal that's  committee chairwoman carolyn maloney  reacting to her own investigators  findings into how mattel and subsidiary  fisher-price  developed and sold the rock and play in  klein's sleeper  we have to take steps to make sure that  this does not happen  again the subcommittee's report obtained  exclusively by cbs news  says fisher-price failed to ensure the  rock n play was safe before bringing it  to market  and ignored critical warnings that the  product was dangerous  pediatricians say babies must sleep on a  flat surface on their backs  but the rock and play sleeper put  infants at an angle of 30 degrees  now the report finds when the product  was launched in 2009  there was no independent research or  even internal company research  showing it was safe for babies to sleep  at an angle  something pediatric injury expert dr ben  hoffman finds disturbing  the fact that that there was no due  diligence done  in talking to experts to even  understanding what safe sleep was and  how  the incline sleeper product operated  completely  counter to what we know safe sleep to be  the report says in october 2012 a mother  reported to the company that her  two-month-old son had stopped breathing  in the sleeper  he was revived but two months later  fisher-price was notified that a 15-week  old infant  died in the rock and play does that pain  ever go away  no no no it's been 10 years and i still  i still cry sarah thompson's 15 week old  son alexander  also died in 2011 after napping in a  rock and play  leaving without him was so hard to come  home with  a car seat in the back and no baby in it  probably the worst day of my life  thompson says she contacted the consumer  product safety commission with no result  in fact the report says it wasn't until  2018  that cpsc staff counted 17 infant deaths  and became  alarmed one writing in an email holy cow  we need to discuss this when the  commission sees this  they are going to flip but the voluntary  recall of the rock and play did not  happen  until a little over a year later because  of what investigators call  grave flaws in the u.s consumer product  safety system  in which manufacturers are largely left  to police themselves  it's supposed to be the consumer product  safety commission  and everything we've learned is  the manufacturers are the ones protected  fisher-price told us they disagree with  significant parts of the report's  findings  the company said the rock and play  sleeper was designed and developed  following extensive research  medical advice safety analysis and more  than a year of testing and review  and that it met or exceeded all  applicable regulatory standards  but chairwoman maloney says we have to  hold corporations responsible  we have to put people over profits  the thompsons are suing fisher-price and  mattel fisher-price told  us the rock and play sleeper was safe  when used in accordance with warnings  and instructions  now the acting chairman of the cpsc says  there's a provision in the law something  called section 6b  which basically means for them that it  undermines the agency's ability to warn  consumers  about dangerous products and it should  be repealed that's undoubtedly going to  be a topic of conversation today  at a congressional hearing later on all  of this meanwhile fisher-price is  recalling  other baby sleep products this morning  the four-in-one  rock and glide soother was linked to  reports of four  infant deaths the children all between  two and four months old were reportedly  put  on their backs in the soother  unrestrained and later found  on their stomachs the company is also  recalling  it's two-in-one soothe-and-play gliders  though no deaths have been reported in  connection with that product  a price official said the deaths  underscore the importance of following  safety instructions  but again tony as you know when a baby  turns over and they are this young  or they turn their head to the side or  drop their head  in that inclined sleeper they don't have  the muscle strength  to roll back over many times or pick  their head back up yeah  it's a tragedy for the family still a  mystery to me how it took more than 30  infant deaths for these products to come  off the market and more than a decade  with them on the market  i'm glad something's happening now  though anna thank you very much

